1
00:06:38,823 --> 00:06:44,823
Their only weapon is the truth.

2
00:13:17,647 --> 00:13:23,647
5 Days of War is a war, drama film directed by Renny Harlin.

3
00:19:56,470 --> 00:20:02,470
An American journalist and his cameraman are caught in the combat zone
during the first Russian airstrikes against Georgia.

4
00:26:35,294 --> 00:26:41,294
Rescuing Tatia, a young Georgian schoolteacher separated from her family during the attack, the two
reporters agree to help reunite her with her family in exchange for serving as their interpreter.

5
00:33:14,117 --> 00:33:20,117
As the three attempt to escape to safety, they witness--and document--the devastation from
the full-scale crossfire and cold-blooded murder of innocent civilians.

6
00:39:52,941 --> 00:39:58,941
Thomas Anders, played by Rupert Friend.

7
00:46:31,764 --> 00:46:37,764
Tatia Meddevi, played by Emmanuelle Chriqui.

8
00:53:10,588 --> 00:53:16,588
Sebastian Ganz, played by Richard Coyle.

9
00:59:49,411 --> 00:59:55,411
Miriam, played by Heather Graham.

10
01:06:28,235 --> 01:06:34,235
Capt. Rezo Avaliani, played by Johnathon Schaech.

11
01:13:07,058 --> 01:13:13,058
Col. Demidov, played by Rade Šerbedžija.

12
01:19:45,882 --> 01:19:51,882
5 Days of War is a 2011 war film directed by Renny Harlin.

13
01:26:24,705 --> 01:26:30,705
The story is about the Russo-Georgian War over the Russian-backed breakaway autonomous republic
of South Ossetia in Georgia, including the events leading up to the conflict.

14
01:33:03,529 --> 01:33:09,529
The film was released in Georgia as 5 Days of August, and in other
countries as 5 Days of War and also City on Fire.

15
01:39:42,352 --> 01:39:48,352
The film explores themes of journalist, war crimes,
mass murder, evacuation, interpreter.

16
01:46:21,176 --> 01:46:27,176
The tone is emotional.
